{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_05d6bdc3e5773285652d03c4ba217cb812ec8c5aba095d360f82cbead36ea600","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"prime-radiant-inc/evener@ea6649c17c5d snapshot afd5117241fc1a76","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_15cb257c397088ee08cd1407394fa701d80dacaf32c73981578d1c519398a57b","slc_864243eaa71fc81de120d133cc498979dad879eafc0e4f44c2f34a9186c4c5c9","slc_cae37152b37a5cbddea6787fe7f6955f1f27c8bdebbf37fff7ffa48ef91fcb53"],"source_ids":["src_134aa3dc632d58ad8d4cf70206afabfc","src_34c1c53002675694bec3f841a8e20ef7","src_fc78730611355cb395e737454298674c"],"text":"A session's file, process, and network access can be confined with the `--sandbox` flag; sandbox denials can escalate to a human approval card, though breaker-parked calls carry no typed error and do not trigger that escalation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3d355114fdce40a8f21bda6bcdc69d4727db0ad03fedca4475e55a14a576a809","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"prime-radiant-inc/evener@ea6649c17c5d snapshot afd5117241fc1a76","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0ca662a1c3cacc4cc0f598b2440ce42fc21ffc95e9d9b5a6271c1a2606024579","slc_b4050e00b444e8f83d9272d4283914fe44ab27956cdd53216774535cd21013e3","slc_f0f1d9cde10f0c07d16d522ebec7abbc02a5eb30c72a4ae3b3e4b153ff86a6e7","slc_fb453d89a93e61be080069aa32a1272590d8615226c4d47b15d387fe1d0e1ce2"],"source_ids":["src_fc78730611355cb395e737454298674c"],"text":"The TUI connects to the hub at 127.0.0.1:9180 by default, auto-starts a missing local hub (unless --no-auto-start-hub), and supports flags like --hub-addr, --hub-bin, --auth-token, --state-dir, and --debug.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_654a61ee0e3f88d56d50d7683e80dfb08c545707cc4f5461c1f617566d80b523","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"prime-radiant-inc/evener@ea6649c17c5d snapshot afd5117241fc1a76","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_000a2d908f1cbb229c0316b49bcc6e2190d8952bfafe9ff252fc3af3b5297263","slc_06c2a14dbdb8dc78426614ab97137533b16237e7086dcae56ee6b1c7f662c8f1","slc_0dfc749c99cc5aaae413cc7af5fb7237403c47d80c7a4adad0aaf735dd07db45","slc_11dfa1867c5a4604f9b6363bc15486621dcd98276d141ff9af1330f8a56d1434","slc_5d66b16b8736aa3a3e818fef539e6a140eb3392d156f97b965196ff725675ff7","slc_f0f2d2548219a25e53c802dbc392d64b8034af11aad51959b285f2980c074db9"],"source_ids":["src_34c1c53002675694bec3f841a8e20ef7"],"text":"The repo is a multi-module Go monorepo (llm, agent, auth libraries plus the app) where binaries couple only via the appwire and hubapi wire contracts, never by importing each other's code; libraries may never import app code.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_754b04d96a8d39a7ee420c1d88bdff1477f7f20ff5887e454e41608f0171b21b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"prime-radiant-inc/evener@ea6649c17c5d snapshot afd5117241fc1a76","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_40d8dc0141fbe69691e5a7d3fdbc5d653badbe80c3a15e4cfbd89a461a4d8a23","slc_5978091cb2c2e125d93739748026e96f9098e409543a9646a9120c33790fa68d","slc_8bd960d308b57e3777ddc3960c805e056f885e1f4c392a5309c5111596813c56","slc_9379f64928e32cdceb3b07362db9c34da755fee86ea7b693e9eff2edafa7db3f"],"source_ids":["src_fc78730611355cb395e737454298674c"],"text":"The hub listens on 127.0.0.1:9180, prints a one-time auth URL that sets an authorizing browser cookie, and offers a /new session page, /credentials page, fork-from-message, /aside side threads, transparent resume, and Ctrl/⌘K search.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c51b98fc026589a199eae4382c2a44cb6fc82d1211e4a120f52915722e8fffca","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"prime-radiant-inc/evener@ea6649c17c5d snapshot afd5117241fc1a76","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_14c5d1b9be6fde77ac8fbb62d999ffdc86e5c220d7271a81b8275100786fcf49","slc_6c23461adedbf9c275d884b07bd5293729f61a79f77f8c8103286a826013e88a","slc_cae37152b37a5cbddea6787fe7f6955f1f27c8bdebbf37fff7ffa48ef91fcb53"],"source_ids":["src_134aa3dc632d58ad8d4cf70206afabfc","src_fc78730611355cb395e737454298674c"],"text":"Evener uses the LLM's native tool-calling and supports many providers out of the box (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Ollama, Bedrock, Azure, and others), with additional providers addable via a providers.toml entry.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d45761b153f2cb18e5ce95b0921689ea546962d172285ce75e3bf1e4b11ece37","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"prime-radiant-inc/evener@ea6649c17c5d snapshot afd5117241fc1a76","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_017e23d2dee15c590caf429ddfd3b167d63ca5d63f9e33c1beb18a512fd8e395","slc_0b2c2d856f9c85d7baa03434668d53ad3cd856f0711af6306960894e0f9580bf"],"source_ids":["src_34c1c53002675694bec3f841a8e20ef7"],"text":"A repeated-call breaker keys a per-session ledger on tool name plus a hash of raw argument bytes: the third consecutive same-class failure is refused before dispatch, and a repetition trigger nudges on byte-identical result bodies without refusing, so communicate is never blocked.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e1c8cec03779524b7f3a45eeca9ec9d5e0cb7c932671b71e5f04114074e3e9ef","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"prime-radiant-inc/evener@ea6649c17c5d snapshot afd5117241fc1a76","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_273d9af68beb19f8b80897d5b38fe77a96ee0fbaf30d0bed3a0e9bdc3251f8af","slc_32b782db70cce67be4d2ee8053df6e8054f906f10b358146821adfda64a47d65","slc_5214de2fc585b1e1ac8c39cfd697950d358247340111c99963c1f0ab8c6e2bc4","slc_5c4741f389fe2a85f899910776d49318c522e57f672a6ba671155a18487e2119","slc_a7865e112097cca554e7fff5100a8325cee964ead67780005de0debc9ce41b85","slc_b55d0d7776d12e22f0ddbc4b9622c363f7b913c9d565f38b4da80fbf8967c16a"],"source_ids":["src_fc78730611355cb395e737454298674c"],"text":"Session state auto-saves under the XDG state directory per project after each assistant turn; project IDs derive from the canonical path so linked worktrees share a bucket while separate clones get distinct ones; sessions resume via --resume, --resume-last, or --resume-with.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e39ec22e5226f349325ada2f2245bd79363453b103fb8cfbca64dc15b890d8ad","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"prime-radiant-inc/evener@ea6649c17c5d snapshot afd5117241fc1a76","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0822f5dc1e9ba3bb597adf1be9edd254e583463266ab994a84792340d0d86f8e","slc_11dfa1867c5a4604f9b6363bc15486621dcd98276d141ff9af1330f8a56d1434","slc_2653b5b4599ead6ccd4114709d6979f2cabdceb67b49029276bf8299eac389af","slc_4a89fc0278f1a3ccc079fdf34368f29e88f15f4c574fa47b0a1f8040430b1ff0","slc_c30dd905db998ec0f1dab54ff0c947b09a63e56fe6fe7b0afefe29532f637aaa","slc_db7f0f5879dbc68b437c7b3f35d95e6eb74bb36ec40b508899d15588d39b4f1d"],"source_ids":["src_34c1c53002675694bec3f841a8e20ef7","src_fc78730611355cb395e737454298674c"],"text":"The product ships three binaries: `evener` (non-interactive CLI engine), `evener hub` (browser-based orchestrator for many concurrent sessions), and `evener tui` (terminal dashboard), plus a one-shot `llmcall` client.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_eab9a401a6711dd8f35704d5ba0b01c788c8aec110fa38cab10f7127fa452d14","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"prime-radiant-inc/evener@ea6649c17c5d snapshot afd5117241fc1a76","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_000a2d908f1cbb229c0316b49bcc6e2190d8952bfafe9ff252fc3af3b5297263","slc_8bd960d308b57e3777ddc3960c805e056f885e1f4c392a5309c5111596813c56","slc_c30dd905db998ec0f1dab54ff0c947b09a63e56fe6fe7b0afefe29532f637aaa"],"source_ids":["src_34c1c53002675694bec3f841a8e20ef7","src_fc78730611355cb395e737454298674c"],"text":"The hub spawns `evener` serve daemons as subprocesses and serves clients over AppWire; sessions can be forked at any user message or to a side thread via /aside, and subagents appear indented under their spawning session in the sidebar.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","created_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ed65f4826fbd15098381a2412f26f5aa61cef47dbefcd72465100213b9177e7c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=skills-patterns","setting":"prime-radiant-inc/evener@ea6649c17c5d snapshot afd5117241fc1a76","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_32b782db70cce67be4d2ee8053df6e8054f906f10b358146821adfda64a47d65","slc_a89fc061981b80b41794b5bc49bf84613437ac26b1a50db046cc57b1398d0a40"],"source_ids":["src_fc78730611355cb395e737454298674c"],"text":"Standalone user skills in the config skills directory are discovered automatically, extra skill paths can be added via skills_dirs in launch.toml or CLI flags, and user-global slash commands are read from a commands directory when present.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:32:56Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f587bc7c40f047d9b97a9af140e585e4"}
